# Technical Standards

## 1. Performance & Rendering
- **Server Components:** Use React Server Components (RSC) by default. The site is a stateless utility; maximize speed by pre-rendering everything.
- **Static Site Generation (SSG):** All 2,000+ fix pages must be statically generated at build time to ensure sub-second load times.
- **Image Optimization:** Always use the Next.js `Image` component with descriptive alt tags for trust signals.
- **Clean Styling:** Use Tailwind CSS. Strictly avoid inline styles.

## 2. Privacy-First & Monetization Readiness
- **Stateless Architecture:** No local user database, no login system, and no local session cookies. 
- **Monetization Guardrails:** Prepare for Google AdSense and Affiliate links by ensuring the layout has "Ad Slots" that do not shift the content (preventing Layout Shift/CLS).
- **Script Loading:** Third-party scripts (AdSense/Affiliates) must be loaded with `next/script` using the `strategy="lazyOnload"` to keep the "One-Minute Fix" interactive immediately.

## 3. Core Web Vitals (The $10k Requirement)
- **LCP (Largest Contentful Paint):** The "One-Minute Fix" code box must be visible in the first frame.
- **CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift):** All ad placeholders must have fixed heights to prevent the page from jumping when ads load.
- **Mobile-Responsive:** All technical code blocks and tables must be 100% horizontal-scroll friendly on mobile.